Task 1: Get the current Bitcoin price in INR using CoinGecko:-

API endpoint

GET https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/simple/price?ids=bitcoin&vs_currencies=inr
Steps in Postman
1. Open Postman and create a new GET request.
2. Enter the endpoint above.
3. Open the Headers tab.
4. Add the API key header required by your CoinGecko account. For CoinGecko Demo API keys, the header is typically x-cg-demo-api-key. Use the header specified for your account.
5. Click Send.
Example header:
Key	Value
x-cg-demo-api-key	{{coingecko_api_key}}
Create the coingecko_api_key variable in your Postman environment and set its value locally.

Expected response structure:

{
  "bitcoin": {
    "inr": 0000000
  }
}

Task 2: Authenticate with Spotify and fetch your profile:-


const accessToken = "YOUR_SPOTIFY_ACCESS_TOKEN";

async function getSpotifyProfile() {
    const response = await fetch("https://api.spotify.com/v1/me", {
        method: "GET",
        headers: {
            Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}`
        }
    });

    if (response.status === 401) {
        console.error("Error: Unauthorized. Check your Spotify access token.");
        return;
    }

    if (!response.ok) {
        console.error("Request failed:", response.status);
        return;
    }

    const profile = await response.json();

    console.log("Spotify profile:");
    console.log("Display name:", profile.display_name);
    console.log("User ID:", profile.id);
    console.log("Email:", profile.email ?? "Not available");
}

getSpotifyProfile().catch(console.error);


